# Code

- TypeScript strict. `any`, `@ts-ignore`, and non-null assertions need a one-line reason in the review, not in a silencer comment.
- Server Components by default. `"use client"` goes on the leaf that uses state, events, or browser APIs.
- Named exports. Default export only in Next.js route files (`page`, `layout`, `route`, `error`, `loading`, `not-found`).
- Component file is `PascalCase.tsx`. Everything else is `kebab-case.ts`. Props type is `SomethingProps` next to the component.
- Data loading lives in an `api` segment and returns typed data. UI does not call `fetch`.
- Secrets stay on the server. Public env vars go through `shared/config`, never read as `process.env` inside UI.
- One `h1` per page. Interactive controls have an accessible name. Layout is mobile-first.
- Full rules: `docs/conventions.md`.
